    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "McDonald Property, Lucan's longest-established Auctioneers, Valuers and Estate Agents, are delighted to present this rare opportunity to acquire a four-bedroom home in the heart of Lucan Village.\r\n\r\nOccupying a highly desirable position within this ever-popular residential estate, No. 2 Sarsfield Park enjoys a wonderful outlook over an attractive amenity green, with mature trees to the front providing privacy and a peaceful sense of tranquillity.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hallway, reception room, kitchen and a particularly versatile utility room, thoughtfully configured to provide convenient access to both the front and rear of the property. Upstairs there are four bedrooms (three double bedrooms) and a family bathroom.\r\n\r\nExternally, the property benefits from a generous poured-concrete driveway to the front, complemented by a raised flower bed planted with a selection of mature plants. To the rear lies a private, beautifully maintained garden, predominantly laid in lawn and bordered by established flower beds. A timber garden shed provides useful additional storage.\r\n\r\nThe location is undoubtedly one of the property's greatest attractions. Situated within easy walking distance of Lucan Village, residents can enjoy a wide range of amenities including excellent schools, shops, cafs, restaurants, pubs and the recently improved Lucan Village Green and Lucan Promenade. The property also benefits from excellent transport links, with regular bus services nearby and convenient access to the N4 road network, providing ease of access to Dublin City and surrounding areas.\r\n\r\nAn excellent opportunity to acquire a four-bedroom home in a mature and highly sought-after location, with the scope to extend and create a wonderful home in the heart of Lucan Village. Viewing is highly recommended.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nAccommodation\r\n\r\nEntrance Hallway: 3.77m x 1.89m with laminate wood floor, composite front door, wood floor and alarm point.\r\n\r\nReception Room: 3.78m x 3.77m with laminate wood floor and feature fireplace\r\n\r\nKitchen: 4.91m x 2.42m with tiled floor, fitted kitchen cabinets and cupboard.\r\n\r\nUtility Room: 5.88m x 1.87m (L-shaped) with tiled floor, fitted cabinet, countertop and overhead shelving. Access from front and access to rear.\r\n\r\nUpstairs\r\n\r\nBedroom 1: 3.78m x 3.29m (average) with carpet and fitted wardrobes and drawers. To front.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2: 4.37m x 2.45m with carpet. To rear.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3: 3.73m x 2.20m with carpet. To front.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4: 2.77m x 2.38m with carpet and fitted shelving. To front.\r\n\r\nBathroom: 2.48m x 1.40m with tiled floor, WC, WHB, partially tiled walls, heated towel rail and shower enclosure T90z.\r\n\r\nLanding: with ladder attic access.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nFeatures\r\n\r\nOil fired central heating.\r\n\r\nVillage location.\r\n\r\nDouble glazed windows.\r\n\r\nPotential to extend.\r\n\r\nNot overlooked to front.\r\n\r\nSt. Mary's Parish.\r\n\r\nWithin a short stroll of local pre-schools, primary and secondary schools.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nMeasurements provided are approximate and intended for guidance. Descriptions, photographs and floor plans are provided for illustrative and guidance purposes. Errors, omissions, inaccuracies, or mis-descriptions in these materials do not entitle any party to claims, actions, or compensation against McDonald Property or the vendor. Prospective buyers or interested parties are responsible for conducting their own due diligence, inspections, or other inquiries to verify the accuracy of the information provided. McDonald Property have not tested any appliances, apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Prospective buyers or interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items."
      },
